# Shell scripts and the Dockerfile MUST keep LF endings.
#
# Git on Windows will happily check these out with CRLF, and Linux then fails to
# run them — the shebang becomes "#!/usr/bin/env bash\r", which resolves to no
# such interpreter. The error Docker prints ("exec format error", or a file that
# plainly exists reported as not found) says nothing about line endings, so this
# is worth pinning rather than debugging later.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/** text eol=lf
